{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages","id":1500941,"title":"Consilium/Order Status, requisitions and new Mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-21T09:05:30-08:00","id":1500941,"title":"Consilium/Order Status, requisitions and new Mages","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Some questions, mainly (but no only) about Consilium / Order Status:<ul><li>By adding a +2 to the availability rating, some requisitions can be made permanent.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Do those become part of your merits dot covered by Sanctity of Merits?</b> e.g Elona has Order Status (Free Council) 5, she request permanent Alternate Identity 3, Resources 3, Safe Place 3. Did she gain 9 merit dots?</li> <li>I<b>f you requisition permanent items and change orders, what happens with your merit dots gained this way? </b></li> </ol></li> </ul><ul><li>When you start as mage as described in Signs of Sorcery, you only gain Wisdom 8, Gnosis 1, 3 dots of Ruling Arcana and the capacity to gain a Praxis:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>If you join an Order in game do you gain High Speech, Order Status, a dot of Occult, rote specialties, and 3 rotes for free or do you have to buy them with XP?</b></li> <li><b>If you had a Tyrannical Awakening, you gain the Exarchal Dream condition and a free dot in Seers of the Throne status. Can you shed that dot (as per Sanctity of merits) or it is permanent in your sheet? </b><br /> <br /> Because if you can not shed that dot, the Tyrannical Awakening guys can never get rid of the condition:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Seers have already sworn themselves to the Exarchs, and as<br /> such <b>add their dots in Seers of the Throne Status to their Notice</b><br /> upon gaining this Condition\u200b. A Seer or a character who had a<br /> Tyrannic Awakening can <b>never reduce his Notice below his<br /> dots in that Merit\u200b</b>&quot;</i></li> </ol></li> </ul><br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-21-2023, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T10:43:21-08:00","id":1500947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages#post1500941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do those become part of your merits dot covered by Sanctity of Merits?[/B] e.g Elona has Order Status (Free Council) 5, she request permanent Alternate Identity 3, Resources 3, Safe Place 3. Did she gain 9 merit dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>You gain Merit dots. You do not get refunded Experiences you never spent if you lose those Merit dots.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you requisition permanent items and change orders, what happens with your merit dots gained this way? </div> </div> </div>Depends on the specific Merits and the circumstances of the change in Order. Defecting from the Seers probably won't let you keep your Mentor, but if you transfer from the Arrow to the Mysterium on good terms you can probably keep your Familiar for long enough to conceivably raise your Death/Mind/Spirit spirit enough to cast the spell yourself if it's dispelled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you join an Order in game do you gain High Speech, Order Status, a dot of Occult, rote specialties, and 3 rotes for free or do you have to buy them with XP? </div> </div> </div>The Newly Awakened Mage Template is for representing newly Awakened mages in play or beginning a chronicle with a completely inexperienced mage, whereas the default template of a mage belonging to an Order who's been Awakened for months at least and undergone basic training.<br /> <br /> If you're playing through Order training you buy your Order benefits with Experiences like you would other Merits \u2014 Rote specialties come with the dot of Order Status like they would with the third dot of Mystery Cult Initiation in a Nameless Order, but if you're not jumping straight to the fully-trained template during downtime you don't get the full benefits of training instantaneously any more than playing out your Awakening in an Adyton averts the need to spend Experiences to buy your first dot of Gnosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you had a Tyrannical Awakening, you gain the Exarchal Dream condition and a free dot in Seers of the Throne status. Can you shed that dot (as per Sanctity of merits) or it is permanent in your sheet?<br /> <br /> Because if you can not shed that dot, the Tyrannical Awakening guys can never get rid of the condition: </div> </div> </div>Full understanding of an Iron Seal Aede allows you to remove the Exarchal Dreams Condition. Depending on how your ST interprets the effects of Tyrannical Awakening, you might need to mess around in another Awakening to get rid of the Status effects, but given that Exarchal Dreams only increments its counter when you draw upon the Exarchs as Yantras the inability to zero out the Notice meter is otherwise a moot point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-21-2023, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T11:25:08-08:00","id":1500951,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> thanks for the answers. I put some comments and questions, be aware that is English not my first language so I might need a bit of detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages?p=1500947#post1500947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You gain Merit dots. You do not get refunded Experiences you never spent if you lose those Merit dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could do what Vampire does for Oath granted merits, and mark them with half a dot in the sheet, so you know that you use the, but not get refunded.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages?p=1500947#post1500947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the specific Merits and the circumstances of the change in Order. Defecting from the Seers probably won't let you keep your Mentor, but if you transfer from the Arrow to the Mysterium on good terms you can probably keep your Familiar for long enough to conceivably raise your Death/Mind/Spirit spirit enough to cast the spell yourself if it's dispelled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages?p=1500947#post1500947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Newly Awakened Mage Template is for representing newly Awakened mages in play or beginning a chronicle with a completely inexperienced mage, whereas the default template of a mage belonging to an Order who's been Awakened for months at least and undergone basic training.<br /> <br /> If you're playing through Order training you buy your Order benefits with Experiences like you would other Merits \u2014 Rote specialties come with the dot of Order Status like they would with the third dot of Mystery Cult Initiation in a Nameless Order, <b>but if you're not jumping straight to the fully-trained template during downtime</b> you don't get the full benefits of training instantaneously any more than playing out your Awakening in an Adyton averts the need to spend Experiences to buy your first dot of Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I highlighted the part that confuses me, do you mean that if the ST wishes to give for free the fully trained template?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages?p=1500947#post1500947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full understanding of an Iron Seal Aede allows you to remove the Exarchal Dreams Condition. Depending on how your ST interprets the effects of Tyrannical Awakening, you might need to mess around in another Awakening to get rid of the Status effects, but given that Exarchal Dreams only increments its counter when you draw upon the Exarchs as Yantras<b> the inability to zero out the Notice meter is otherwise a moot point</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But my question remains, can you refund that merit dot of Seer of the Throne Status? Because if yes, there is another way to remove the Exarchal Dreams condition: lose the status dot AND do not use magic for a while.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>At the start of each chapter, <b>subtract one point of Notice,<br /> and another two if the character did not use magic during the<br /> previous chapter</b>. At the start of a new story, the character\u2019s<br /> Notice resets to 1.</i>&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> If you have the status it is impossible to get to Notice 0, but if you lose the status (refunding the merit), THEN you can not use magic for a while and Notice is substracted from your current value.<br /> <br /> Also, it is not a moot point as Notice + Gnosis has a top value, so eventually a character can gain notice by getting enough Status (Seers) + Gnosis + Yantra usage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T11:28:30-08:00","id":1500952,"title":"","content":"Duplicated Post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Duplicated Post 01-21-2023, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T15:03:25-08:00","id":1500964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1500941-consilium-order-status-requisitions-and-new-mages?p=1500951#post1500951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I highlighted the part that confuses me, do you mean that if the ST wishes to give for free the fully trained template?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that unless you go through an offscreen timeskip between sessions to change the character's starting template from the Newly Awakened Mage Template to the regular Mage Template, you do not get the things the full Mage Template gives you for free from joining an Order in play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But my question remains, can you refund that merit dot of Seer of the Throne Status? </div> </div> </div>It is a function of having a Tyrannic Awakening. Being able to get rid of it would defeat the purpose of a Tyrannic Awakening preventing you from completely getting rid of the mark of the Exarchs without Supernal symbol-surgery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it is not a moot point as Notice + Gnosis has a top value, so eventually a character can gain notice by getting enough Status (Seers) + Gnosis + Yantra usage. </div> </div> </div>Notice <i>is</i> Yantra usage, and if you don't buy more Seer Status or use Patron Yantras the top value is <i>hitting Gnosis 9+</i>, which is not only a deep investment but also an avoidable one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Having Awakened with interference from the Exarchs saddles you with attention that makes drawing on the Exarchs as Yantras \u2014 a practice not advertised as possible by the Pentacle and distrusted by those in the know besides \u2014 draw attention that is difficult to get rid of and requires you to limit the extent of your personal and societal growth in magical circles if you don't instead join the Exarchs' servants willingly or under coercion&quot; is the specific complication you sign up for as a player when you choose to play a character with a Tyrannic Awakening. Short of undoing the Tyrannic aspect of your Awakening, that aspect of the character doesn't go away.<br /> <br /> The single dot of Seer Status represents the Exarchs having graced you with their attention \u2014 belonging to another Order means you can't use that dot for requisitions, so you're just getting an extra Social die against characters a Status 1 Seer would have sway over and treating your Resources as one dot higher for acquiring mundane items or services, and depending on how the ST applies the out-of-Caucus penalty for Order Status it might not even have that much effect.<br /> <br /> Also, the only other aspect of Exarchal Dreams besides the Notice track is that you get Arcane Beats for gaining Notice by using Patron Tools. If you get rid of the Condition through an Iron Seal and then never use Patron Tools more than once a story again the fact that raising your Gnosis while you have the Condition will eventually bring on a Supernal harrowing is irrelevant, because not having the Condition means you're not gaining or risking the harrowing as long as you don't use Patron Tools often enough to regain the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}